{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1414409-ex3-soak-overhaul-and-solar-resistance-rework","id":1414409,"title":"Ex3 Soak Overhaul and Solar Resistance rework","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-09-18T09:17:47-07:00","id":1414409,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon1.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Ex3 Soak Overhaul and Solar Resistance rework","content":"How soak works in Ex3 has bothered me so I decided to give it an overhaul. Soak now allows people to have a significant amount of damage reduction that is geared towards conserving your resources but does so in a way that no longer bogs down the game into 20 turn crawls through the mud where tears of joy are wept if you gain more than 2 initiative on a single attack. Likewise, the rules should be simple enough that you won\u2019t need to rewrite 95% of currently written material (So soak charms from NPCs, other exalts, Martial Arts, sorcery, and all that other jazz should neatly co-exist with this without much issue). It\u2019s overall far less drastic to some of the other fixes I\u2019ve seen, and I feel it\u2019s the best I can do without making Ex4 or rewriting vast swaths of NPCs or other bits of the system.<br /> <br /> Solar Resistance has also been bothering me as well. It suffers from a lack of clarity on its charms, charms that are too effective and bog down gameplay, and some charms that are just don\u2019t impress me. I think each charm a person purchases should be both entertaining to use in-game and serve a useful purpose or niche. Charms that were broken (EX: Essence Gathering Temper) have been nerfed and a small smattering of new Resistance charms. The old Resistance tree worked, but it felt like a rattling bumpy car to me. Hopefully, this new version should be much smoother.<br /> <br /> But enough rambling here's what you came for.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CmchKzwmivds0L8oqH_XO1kkBMmkIYJnW6oWRTfhh5k/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...WRTfhh5k/edit#</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":1183,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","user":"Sandact6","date":". 09-18-2020, 12:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-19T07:57:34-07:00","id":1414565,"title":"","content":"Not read it yet, bue a Soak rework is definitively something I'm happy to see somehow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-19T09:45:42-07:00","id":1414574,"title":"","content":"I'd worry that the cap on soak is past the point where soak matters under most circumstances - a strength 5 person wielding a heavy mortal weapon is still reduced to overwhelming by 15 soak, as is I think anyone else reliant on str+weapon for damage. It seems like this only helps deal damage if you're using damage-boosting charms. Though I wasn't including extra successes in this. Still, anyone except the strength 5, non-balanced, heavy mortal weapon wielder has room for at least 1 extra success before it matter<br /> Given that, there's a broad range of circumstances where this makes high soak better - it's nearly impossible for one person to remove initiative from someone with 15 soak, 5 burner initiative, and fairly easy to remove a small amount of initiative from someone with 25 soak<br /> <br /> How does this interact with soak reduction (ie. piercing attacks, the initial Ebon Shadow Charm, Armor-Piercing Fang Strike)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-19T10:07:05-07:00","id":1414577,"title":"","content":"15 soak is just shy the maximum a person with artifact heavy armour and Stamina 5 can achieve. Heavy weapons with Strength 5 will have a damage of 19 before charms, so even 1 threshold success will end up with 5 damage. If you want a more fair comparison for mortals look at mundane heavy armour and stamina 5, which is a soak of 12 and compare this to a heavy weapon which will have a damage of 16 when used with Strength 5. Artifact weapons and armour are nearly a different tier, and often much more effective to those things below it by virtue of math alone before adding in other bonuses.<br /> <br /> If you\u2019re worried about how high 15 soak is, then yes you typically will have to invest in damage charms in order to damage those people. More of often than not those people will be likely be using magic or other investments in order to increase their soak that high.<br /> <br /> Also flip the thought you had in your head. The idea wasn\u2019t making a person <i>lose</i> initiative with this rework, the idea was to make it much easier for the other party to <i>gain</i> initiative. It\u2019s much easier to gain initiative from someone with 15 soak 5 burner init than it is against someone who just has 25 soak. Typically the only way past 25 soak are very lucky rolls, post soak builds, or Solar Brawl (Which becomes much less useful when soak goes beyond that). I\u2019d like large amounts of raw damage to be scary again rather than make people go asleep. Likewise Storyteller\u2019s won\u2019t need to balloon antagonist damage values so that the thing that challenges the 25 soak character won\u2019t instantly paste the 10 soak character. There\u2019s some wriggle room there at least.<br /> <br /> Soak reduction remains the same, it\u2019s essentially a form of damage increase anyways. As mentioned in the document I haven\u2019t tested this extensively yet.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-19T10:54:18-07:00","id":1414587,"title":"","content":"But a heavy artifact weapon has an overwhelming of 5 or 6, so even with 1 extra success a soak of 15+ is the same as 15. Non-Balanced Heavy Mortal weapons have the highest difference between raw damage and soak of all weapons (besides maybe some charm-generated weapons, I don't want to run the math on Elemental Bolt Attack)<br /> The damage bonus of artifact weapons is basically the same as the overwhelming bonus, so soak is not much more or less effective against artifacts.<br /> <br /> It's only much easier to gain initiative against someone with init 15 if you have pre-soak damage in the 20s.<br /> Are you counting &quot;has a daiklave&quot; as a post-soak build? Because a daiklave gets on average 3.5 initiative from a hit on any soak, and is a pretty low bar to pass for an Exalted. Which is also a way to threaten the a 25 soak character without instantly pasting the 10 soak character (admittedly requiring precise values to do both of those and make the extra 15 soak feel worth the cost)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-19T12:40:45-07:00","id":1414622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>autXautY</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1414409-ex3-soak-overhaul-and-solar-resistance-rework?p=1414587#post1414587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But a heavy artifact weapon has an overwhelming of 5 or 6, so even with 1 extra success a soak of 15+ is the same as 15. Non-Balanced Heavy Mortal weapons have the highest difference between raw damage and soak of all weapons (besides maybe some charm-generated weapons, I don't want to run the math on Elemental Bolt Attack)<br /> The damage bonus of artifact weapons is basically the same as the overwhelming bonus, so soak is not much more or less effective against artifacts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Overwhelming isn\u2019t completely useless. Against those things that can still explictedly raise their soak it is going to still have a use. I want to avoid One True Builds where post soak and Overwhelming stackers are the be-all end-all of combat.<br /> <br /> Also the point here isn\u2019t just armour. It\u2019s far easier in comparison to stack soak boosters along with the massive bonus armour gives to give high soaks. Damage usually has in invest in far more.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>autXautY</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1414409-ex3-soak-overhaul-and-solar-resistance-rework?p=1414587#post1414587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's only much easier to gain initiative against someone with init 15 if you have pre-soak damage in the 20s.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m not sure what point you\u2019re trying to make here. Of course more damage will get you more initiative, but the issue is that soak rapidly outpaces damage in most circumstances. I am also aiming for battle to proceed more quickly with this hack. So rather than get something like 2 or 3 initiative against a soakbeast and then repeat for the 20 or so turns it\u2019d take to get the initiative for a decisive you can instead get something like 6 or more far more easily and consistently but the soakbeast still retains their advantage of initiative.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>autXautY</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1414409-ex3-soak-overhaul-and-solar-resistance-rework?p=1414587#post1414587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you counting &quot;has a daiklave&quot; as a post-soak build?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A daiklave has an average of 2.5 damage per hit, not 3.5. (5/2 = 2.5). Unless you mean a grand daiklave, which has 3.<br /> <br /> And no, I am not counting a daiklave as a post soak build. Here are examples of post soak/overwhelming stacking builds:<ul><li>Solar: Heavy weapon + Fire and Stones Strike. Bring over Immortal Blade for extra damage, or Shining Razor wind from 2e if you want to make a GM cry.</li> <li>Dragonblooded: Heavy Weapon + Demon-Crushing Wolf Bite. Pretty good charm honestly. If you use Crimson Fang Bite with it (and drop the WP cost on it) then it\u2019s a solid good combo.</li> <li>Lunar: Claws of the Silver moon/any animal with high overwhelming/heavy weapon + Ferocious Biting Tooth + Divine Predator Strike. Bit too much RNG for my liking but certainly effective. For obvious reasons this combo really doesn\u2019t kick in until something like Essence 3.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>autXautY</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1414409-ex3-soak-overhaul-and-solar-resistance-rework?p=1414587#post1414587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because a daiklave gets on average <b>2.5</b> initiative from a hit on any soak, and is a pretty low bar to pass for an Exalted. Which is also a way to threaten the a 25 soak character without instantly pasting the 10 soak character (admittedly requiring precise values to do both of those and make the extra 15 soak feel worth the cost)</div> </div> </div> </div>2.5 (or even 3.5) damage does not threaten a soakbeast. Soak is only one issue, they\u2019ll also have charms to reduce that damage. Look at Solar Resistance RAW, it literally halves damage. I\u2019m often lucky to get more than a single point of initiative from an attack.<br /> <br /> Think of this as two parts of a problem. To get a solution to need to fix both of them.<br /> <br /> And no. An enemy that has charms that let\u2019s them get up to 30 damage to threaten the 25 soak character will instantly crush the 10 soak character. A 25 soak character is usually going to have other charms to reduce damage, a character with 10 soak is likely grabbing some armour and calling it a day (Such as an Eclipse or something). They may have few if any charms to help with damage reduction if actually hit. The penalty for being hit in the 10 soak character\u2019s case is enormous.<br /> <br /> Are there ways around this? Yes, I have made them. But I\u2019ve gotten to a point that rather in fiddling in increasing niche scenarios of how to challenge high soak characters I just decided to set a ceiling they can\u2019t break through.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":1183,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","user":"Sandact6","date":". 09-19-2020, 03:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-19T15:10:54-07:00","id":1414656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1414409-ex3-soak-overhaul-and-solar-resistance-rework?p=1414622#post1414622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Overwhelming isn\u2019t completely useless. Against those things that can still explictedly raise their soak it is going to still have a use. I want to avoid One True Builds where post soak and Overwhelming stackers are the be-all end-all of combat.<br /> <br /> Also the point here isn\u2019t just armour. It\u2019s far easier in comparison to stack soak boosters along with the massive bonus armour gives to give high soaks. Damage usually has in invest in far more.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not sure what point you\u2019re trying to make here. Of course more damage will get you more initiative, but the issue is that soak rapidly outpaces damage in most circumstances. I am also aiming for battle to proceed more quickly with this hack. So rather than get something like 2 or 3 initiative against a soakbeast and then repeat for the 20 or so turns it\u2019d take to get the initiative for a decisive you can instead get something like 6 or more far more easily and consistently but the soakbeast still retains their advantage of initiative.<br /> <br /> And no. An enemy that has charms that let\u2019s them get up to 30 damage to threaten the 25 soak character will instantly crush the 10 soak character. A 25 soak character is usually going to have other charms to reduce damage, a character with 10 soak is likely grabbing some armour and calling it a day (Such as an Eclipse or something). They may have few if any charms to help with damage reduction if actually hit. The penalty for being hit in the 10 soak character\u2019s case is enormous.</div> </div> </div> </div>My point is the opposite of Overwhelming being useless. I'm saying overwhelming is the counter-tool to high soak. Very high soak characters are no more useful than high soak characters, because both simply reduce damage to the overwhelming value. You could have soak 40, and still take as much damage from most attacks as someone with soak 15. The way to threaten someone with soak 25, without crushing someone with soak 10, is to give the enemy overwhelming 5+. Which probably leads to them doing about as much damage to the two characters, or a few points more to the one with soak 10. It doesn't matter how easy it is to raise soak, because after a certain point soak is useless.<br /> <br /> Charms that reduce post-soak damage are a problem, but they're a separate concern than soak boosters.<br /> <br /> How are you getting 6 or more initiative with your system? To average 6 initiative with soak 15 you need to have 25 raw damage. That's not absurd, but it's a very damage focused character. Most people will have less than 15 points between their raw damage and their overwhelming, and so will be gaining the same 3 points under both systems.<br /> <br /> Your system does make pre-soak damage boosters stronger against high-soak targets, at the cost of making high-soak target much stronger against everyone else, since it replaces soak that was useless against overwhelming with useful burner initiative. <br /> <br /> I'm not sure, but I think the main One True Build, based on the Arena thread, is immediate decisive attacks. Though, I don't recall any fights between alpha-strike builds and optimized solar defenders, so maybe it isn't. It's great at killing masses of Dragonblooded, at least.<br /> Also, getting enough soak most attacks deal overwhelming is pretty easy, so I expect most builds are going to do it just because they can. Artifact heavy armor costs 6m and 3 merit dots. Unusual Hide 5+mortal heavy armor grants more soak for 0m and 5 merit dots. Either of those +middling stamina will get you to high teens. I expect that high investment in soak will be rare in highly optimized combat, but that cheap investment will get to the point that soak is much higher than in most play (also, appearance tends to be a limiter on soak outside of white rooms - a pestle tail with artifact heavy armor, invulnerable skin of bronze, and unusual hide 5 has 39 soak, without any remarkable investment, but is far from subtle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-19T15:51:06-07:00","id":1414662,"title":"","content":"So now the enemy with 30 raw damage crushes <i>both</i> characters instead of just the lower-soak one. Congrats?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-19T18:06:56-07:00","id":1414672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>autXautY</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1414409-ex3-soak-overhaul-and-solar-resistance-rework?p=1414656#post1414656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My point is the opposite of Overwhelming being useless. I'm saying overwhelming is the counter-tool to high soak. Very high soak characters are no more useful than high soak characters, because both simply reduce damage to the overwhelming value. You could have soak 40, and still take as much damage from most attacks as someone with soak 15. The way to threaten someone with soak 25, without crushing someone with soak 10, is to give the enemy overwhelming 5+. Which probably leads to them doing about as much damage to the two characters, or a few points more to the one with soak 10. It doesn't matter how easy it is to raise soak, because after a certain point soak is useless.</div> </div> </div> </div>I tried that. I have tried that for literal years. The only thing that happens is that post soak/overwhelming builds becoming OTB options. If my overwhelming damage is so high enough to the point to where a character with high soak is on the same footing as the person with low soak, then it feels like my build has just been invalidated. This is going to be especially true if nearly every enemy comes with some way around that. I don\u2019t even blame the storyteller for doing this, as making characters that are challenging, balanced, and don\u2019t immediately invalidate character\u2019s hard earned XP choices is a delicate balance.<br /> I am making another way out One True Build problems.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>autXautY</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1414409-ex3-soak-overhaul-and-solar-resistance-rework?p=1414656#post1414656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Charms that reduce post-soak damage are a problem, but they're a separate concern than soak boosters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Different symptoms of the same problem in my view.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>autXautY</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1414409-ex3-soak-overhaul-and-solar-resistance-rework?p=1414656#post1414656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How are you getting 6 or more initiative with your system? To average 6 initiative with soak 15 you need to have 25 raw damage. That's not absurd, but it's a very damage focused character.</div> </div> </div> </div>You\u2019re right, it is a very damage focused character, but it\u2019s not something outside the realm of feasibility to obtain. My Lunar hits 21 damage easily. If I wanted he soak to be higher it could much higher than her damage. I\u2019m a gentleman and keep it at 15 to lessen my ST\u2019s headaches.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>autXautY</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1414409-ex3-soak-overhaul-and-solar-resistance-rework?p=1414656#post1414656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most people will have less than 15 points between their raw damage and their overwhelming, and so will be gaining the same 3 points under both systems.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except soakbeasts will also have charms that shave off damage, so you\u2019ll be getting less than that. Do you know what I feels like to slam someone with a 30 raw damage attack, them have 16 soak, then only deal 3 damage to them? Do you know how long that makes combat drag out?<br /> <br /> You\u2019re mistaking one aspect for the entire issue when there\u2019s another, equally important issue to look at. Average statistics are a thing, but you need to also keep in mind how wildly charms can cause these values to fluctuate.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d also like it if characters who specced into damage are rewarded for the resources they sink into an attack, a lot more. Raw damage charms shouldn\u2019t worthless things to purchase.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>autXautY</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1414409-ex3-soak-overhaul-and-solar-resistance-rework?p=1414656#post1414656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your system does make pre-soak damage boosters stronger against high-soak targets, at the cost of making high-soak target much stronger against everyone else, since it replaces soak that was useless against overwhelming with useful burner initiative.</div> </div> </div> </div>Soak is massively nerfed. With a hard cap people can no longer laugh off everything and anything unless they came from very specific builds. They still laugh off the attack, but know if they\u2019re hit then the enemy is going to gain some resources from them. Additionally they need to pay attention to numbers, as if one good blow knocks out your burner initiative then it means others can dig into your actual initiative. Either way the combat moves towards a point where someone can make a decisive and KO the other side. They\u2019re forced to take combat seriously.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>autXautY</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1414409-ex3-soak-overhaul-and-solar-resistance-rework?p=1414656#post1414656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure, but I think the main One True Build, based on the Arena thread, is immediate decisive attacks. Though, I don't recall any fights between alpha-strike builds and optimized solar defenders, so maybe it isn't. It's great at killing masses of Dragonblooded, at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m not contesting immediate alpha strike builds, many of the charms I made still reduce or take the teeth out of decisive attacks just fine I feel like. But it\u2019s a major issue when the alpha striker fails to kill their target and said target is a soakbeast. Do you know how trivially high soak shuts down Solar Archery and Thrown? If there\u2019s ever a chance you don\u2019t kill them: You\u2019re hooped. There\u2019s simply no way you\u2019re going to farm meaningful damage out from them as you have essentially 0 withering boosters, and even if you did they mountains of soak make that incredibly hard to do.<br /> With a soak cap of 15, they still run into some issues but they\u2019ll at least have an easier time getting there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>autXautY</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1414409-ex3-soak-overhaul-and-solar-resistance-rework?p=1414656#post1414656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, getting enough soak most attacks deal overwhelming is pretty easy, so I expect most builds are going to do it just because they can. *Snip soak build sample*</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is you only need one PC to make a high soak build before everything becomes annoying complicated. It only takes one PC to start investing in damage resistance and make absurdly high damage builds capable of threatening them, builds that will melt the 10 soak character (who may only have an Ox-Body and Durability of Oak if we\u2019re lucky) like a wielder\u2019s torch to butter. Compare this to a soak cap: I don\u2019t need to make an enemy with absurdly high damages. Anything that can hurt the soakbeast will knock the breath out of the 10 soak dude but not outright vaporize them. Meanwhile the enemy can still farm initiative from the soakbeast and their own pool of burner initiative. Combat progresses, everyone\u2019s happy.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1414409-ex3-soak-overhaul-and-solar-resistance-rework?p=1414662#post1414662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So now the enemy with 30 raw damage crushes <i>both</i> characters instead of just the lower-soak one. Congrats?</div> </div> </div> </div>See the point I raised to autXautY just right above. You won\u2019t need enemies with absurd damages anymore. Things can be a lot more controlled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-21T05:46:57-07:00","id":1414905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1414409-ex3-soak-overhaul-and-solar-resistance-rework?p=1414672#post1414672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is you only need one PC to make a high soak build before everything becomes annoying complicated. It only takes one PC to start investing in damage resistance and make absurdly high damage builds capable of threatening them, builds that will melt the 10 soak character (who may only have an Ox-Body and Durability of Oak if we\u2019re lucky) like a wielder\u2019s torch to butter. Compare this to a soak cap: I don\u2019t need to make an enemy with absurdly high damages. Anything that can hurt the soakbeast will knock the breath out of the 10 soak dude but not outright vaporize them. Meanwhile the enemy can still farm initiative from the soakbeast and their own pool of burner initiative. Combat progresses, everyone\u2019s happy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I must say it was a big problem in my first Campaign. The High Stamina Crafter sorcerer Twilight with 22 Soak or something like that, compared to the other people with 10 Soak. Either I ignored him in battle (which feels bad to do ...) or I did characters with so much damage they were kinda stupid when fighting someone else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-21T07:57:52-07:00","id":1414917,"title":"","content":"The sidereal i play has a presence charm that gives ablative initiative to lose in place of your own when you take damage, and it has a good feel. You are as protected as always, but the battle can go somewhere for the other guy.<br /> <br /> It brings a healthier pace, one that is worth the extra note on your character sheet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-21T08:11:57-07:00","id":1414918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1414409-ex3-soak-overhaul-and-solar-resistance-rework?p=1414917#post1414917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The sidereal i play has a presence charm that gives ablative initiative to lose in place of your own when you take damage, and it has a good feel. You are as protected as always, but the battle can go somewhere for the other guy.<br /> <br /> It brings a healthier pace, one that is worth the extra note on your character sheet.</div> </div> </div> </div>I <i>really</i> like this as a charm mechanic. Will yoink at the first available opportunity. Has it resulted in more memorable fights? More gambits all round, quicker to launch decisives, that kind of thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24647,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","user":"Moss Reynholm","date":". 09-21-2020, 11:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-21T08:59:24-07:00","id":1414924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1414409-ex3-soak-overhaul-and-solar-resistance-rework?p=1414917#post1414917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The sidereal i play has a presence charm that gives ablative initiative to lose in place of your own when you take damage, and it has a good feel. You are as protected as always, but the battle can go somewhere for the other guy.<br /> <br /> It brings a healthier pace, one that is worth the extra note on your character sheet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting to see someone else already tested this. I'm not a fan of the existence of another counter, but it may prove an interesting solution. The best thing would be to find a way to include it more directly into the existing stats on the character sheet, but I doubt it's possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-21T09:22:49-07:00","id":1414930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moss Reynholm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1414409-ex3-soak-overhaul-and-solar-resistance-rework?p=1414918#post1414918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I <i>really</i> like this. Will yoink at the first available opportunity. Has it resulted in more memorable fights? More gambits all round, quicker to launch decisives, that kind of thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not him, but I have tested similar mechanics in my own game, both recently and in the past.<ul><li>On enemies it brings a little worry to the PC's seeing an opponent's initiative being shielded, but it's less frustrating for the players as they don't grumble about doing barely any damage and can actually gain initiative.</li> <li>For players it provides a useful buffer, <i>especially</i> after making a decisive attack. You have room to breathe after making a decisive, but it's still tense as you don't want too many people ganging up at you at once. Gambits are encouraged a little more as you don't need to worry about getting resources from a soakbeast while decisives can be launched more quickly.</li> </ul><br /> It worked very well for the Infernal I had over the weekend, a colosseum free for all in Malfeas where he had an ablative initiative drip of 2/turn. The player seemed to enjoy it very much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-21T09:27:00-07:00","id":1414931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1414409-ex3-soak-overhaul-and-solar-resistance-rework?p=1414924#post1414924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interesting to see someone else already tested this. I'm not a fan of the existence of another counter, but it may prove an interesting solution. The best thing would be to find a way to include it more directly into the existing stats on the character sheet, but I doubt it's possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes the only real downside is having another resource to track on your sheet. For some this is a dealbreaker. Often I had people tell me that between Willpower, motes, damage, soak, and initiative being highly variable in combat it becomes too much for them. But making this one little fix has made things easier for me to plan encounters and more fair to the PC's.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-21T09:34:56-07:00","id":1414932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moss Reynholm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1414409-ex3-soak-overhaul-and-solar-resistance-rework?p=1414918#post1414918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I <i>really</i> like this as a charm mechanic. Will yoink at the first available opportunity. Has it resulted in more memorable fights? More gambits all round, quicker to launch decisives, that kind of thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sandact's commentary is accurate to my experience.<br /> More gambits isn't too much of a thing because gambits aren't all that used in the first place, sadly. Their cost is a secondary concern.<br /> <br /> This is most evident when we talk about hardness. Hardness is a bit underrated because it has to be evaluated with soak in consideration. A soak monster's hardness 10 is amazingly stronger than hardness 10 would be on a guy that just has mid-high soak, because the soak monster has that much more leeway to keep the enemy initiative low.<br /> <br /> Enemies pinging all the time easily need 4-5 rounds of hitting without being hit back before their base initiative raises past 10. With this ablation mechanic sandact proposes (and I use in sidereals and will use when I finally get around to the resistance remake) it's more of a 1-3 rounds consideration. mid-power decisives gain some oomph with this, round-by-round dynamics are a bit more varied.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-21T12:54:38-07:00","id":1414954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1414409-ex3-soak-overhaul-and-solar-resistance-rework?p=1414931#post1414931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes the only real downside is having another resource to track on your sheet. For some this is a dealbreaker. Often I had people tell me that between Willpower, motes, damage, soak, and initiative being highly variable in combat it becomes too much for them. But making this one little fix has made things easier for me to plan encounters and more fair to the PC's.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I understand. I'd really like to get rid of WP at some point, seems too much like WoD legacy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-21T14:14:47-07:00","id":1414966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1414409-ex3-soak-overhaul-and-solar-resistance-rework?p=1414954#post1414954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I understand. I'd really like to get rid of WP at some point, seems too much like WoD legacy</div> </div> </div> </div>Already on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-22T01:03:38-07:00","id":1415026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1414409-ex3-soak-overhaul-and-solar-resistance-rework?p=1414932#post1414932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sandact's commentary is accurate to my experience.<br /> More gambits isn't too much of a thing because gambits aren't all that used in the first place, sadly. Their cost is a secondary concern.<br /> <br /> This is most evident when we talk about hardness. Hardness is a bit underrated because it has to be evaluated with soak in consideration. A soak monster's hardness 10 is amazingly stronger than hardness 10 would be on a guy that just has mid-high soak, because the soak monster has that much more leeway to keep the enemy initiative low.<br /> <br /> Enemies pinging all the time easily need 4-5 rounds of hitting without being hit back before their base initiative raises past 10. With this ablation mechanic sandact proposes (and I use in sidereals and will use when I finally get around to the resistance remake) it's more of a 1-3 rounds consideration. mid-power decisives gain some oomph with this, round-by-round dynamics are a bit more varied.</div> </div> </div> </div>It might necessitate a thread of its own, but wouldn't integrating Gambits in Decisive attacks directly be a good idea to make gambits more interesting ? Like you just make a normal decisive attack, and if you want you can transform X damage into gambit Y, where the cost of Y is X. You can chose so at your discretion after succeeding the decisive attack, and if you don't you of course deal damage as normal. Any excess initiative beyond X stayed as normal damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-22T06:07:00-07:00","id":1415053,"title":"","content":"Yes. There's a few ways to make gambits more interesting. In order of importance, to me: Action cost, Unnecessary roll and Initiative cost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-22T06:55:53-07:00","id":1415063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1414409-ex3-soak-overhaul-and-solar-resistance-rework?p=1414930#post1414930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not him, but I have tested similar mechanics in my own game, both recently and in the past.<ul><li>On enemies it brings a little worry to the PC's seeing an opponent's initiative being shielded, but it's less frustrating for the players as they don't grumble about doing barely any damage and can actually gain initiative.</li> <li>For players it provides a useful buffer, <i>especially</i> after making a decisive attack. You have room to breathe after making a decisive, but it's still tense as you don't want too many people ganging up at you at once. Gambits are encouraged a little more as you don't need to worry about getting resources from a soakbeast while decisives can be launched more quickly.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> It worked very well for the Infernal I had over the weekend, a colosseum free for all in Malfeas where he had an ablative initiative drip of 2/turn. The player seemed to enjoy it very much.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice, thanks both to you and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar32_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"32\" data-vbnamecard=\"32\">Synapse</a>. Feels especially Sidereal-ly as a mechanic \u2013 &quot;You thought your furious offensive had placed me at a disadvantage? Wrong, I was actually opening a hole in your defence the entire time&quot; etc etc.<br /> <br /> I think our group would collectively scream if we tried to fiddle with soak at this point in our current game having barely got our heads around RAW, but the tweaks in OP look intriguing. Kudos. Maybe the next one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24647,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","user":"Moss Reynholm","date":". 09-22-2020, 09:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}